Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Task 43 — keep local secrets out of the image build entirely.
#
# The builder stage is a bare `COPY . .`, so an untracked `.env.local` on the developer's
# disk was being copied into a build layer, where `next build` would additionally INLINE
# its NEXT_PUBLIC_* values into the shipped client bundle. The runner stage never copies
# it forward, so the final image was clean — but the build layer was not, and the bundle
# carried whichever redirect URL that particular laptop happened to have.
#
# Nothing is lost by excluding it: YV_APP_KEY reaches the container as a RUNTIME env from
# the compose `nextjs` service (D43.3), and `app/providers.tsx`'s `||` fallback is exactly
# the mechanism that makes an unset build-time NEXT_PUBLIC_YV_AUTH_REDIRECT_URL resolve to
# the runtime origin.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
